# ── DigiHRMS AI Copilot (beta) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Append these lines to the real .env on the server (digihrms/.env).
# Pick ONE provider — set the key + base URL + model together, don't mix them.

# ── Option A: NVIDIA NIM (recommended — generous free rate limits) ────────
# Key: https://build.nvidia.com  → open a model with "Function Calling" → Get API Key
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=nvapi-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
# other NVIDIA options: nvidia/llama-3.1-nemotron-70b-instruct , deepseek-ai/deepseek-v3.1
# Verify the exact slug on the model's page — NVIDIA retires old ones (HTTP 410).

# ── Option B: OpenRouter ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys   Model slugs: https://openrouter.ai/models?q=free
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free
# NOTE: free OpenRouter models rate-limit hard (429) — the agent makes several
# calls per message. Add $10 credit for 1000/day, or use NVIDIA.

# ── Option C: local Ollama on the LAN (only if HRMS can reach the box) ───
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=ollama
#OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:11434/v1
#OPENROUTER_MODEL=llama3.1

# ── Table scope (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Copilot is hard-limited to task & workflow tables; anything else is blocked.
# Override the lists only if the defaults miss a table name in your schema.
#AI_AGENT_WRITE_TABLES=tasks,task_comments,task_time_logs,projects,hrms_triggers,hrms_workflow_runs
# Extra tables the agent may SELECT (never write). Empty = task/workflow only.
#AI_AGENT_READ_TABLES=users,employees,departments
